  "title": "# RESUME: molly-banner-match Brett paused this so the merge queue could land, then said \"start buil…",
  "asked": "# RESUME: molly-banner-match Brett paused this so the merge queue could land, then said \"start building\". **The spec is `/root/axf-builds/molly-banner-match/.brief.md`. Read it first.** Your branch starts from the saved WIP (it had only run ~2 minutes). Check the tail of `/root/axf-builds/molly-banner-match/molly-banner-match.log` and continue. - Keep the store entry as `molly-banner-match` (no duplicate). Book to Ping Paulie or any free agent. - PRs go **through the merge queue only**. Auto-land is OFF. Basic Markdown readme. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM (Brett, voice, Nov 4) - DO FIRST \"The approval waiting pop-up when I'm in Molly shows the sad face, but not when I'm in console.\" - The Follow Amber approval pop-up (dialog `follow-amber.approval`) crashes to the error face ONLY in the console embedded in Molly (client host=molly, app molly/console-web). It works in the standalone console. - Joey's urgent-approval-popup-crash fix (fallback screen, chunk-reload) assumed Molly needed no change. Check whether that PR is merged/deployed. Then reproduce inside Molly's embed and fix the real cause. Likely suspects: the pop-up tries to frame axHub's approvals page and Molly's origin isn't allowed (AXHUB_APPROVALS_FRAME_ANCESTORS / CSP frame-ancestors), embed@1 hides something the pop-up depends on, cross-origin/cookie access from inside Molly's iframe, or Molly serving a stale console bundle. - The pop-up must never crash in either place. If framing isn't allowed it falls back to Approve/Deny buttons plus an 'Open in axHub' button. - Add a regression test that runs the pop-up inside a Molly-style embed. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
